## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Dual-Stream Architecture (same as Model 2):** Reuses the identical `DualStreamBLIP2` wrapper — shared frozen ViT + Q-Former encodes $T_1$ and $T_2$ independently, concatenates their 32-token query outputs → 64 visual tokens → LoRA-adapted OPT-2.7B. No new layers needed.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Synthetic Bi-Temporal Pairs:** For the prototype, temporal changes are **synthesised** from real EuroSAT images by applying controlled transformations simulating realistic change scenarios:
> - **Urbanisation:** Green areas → added building-like structures, grey patches
> - **Deforestation:** Dense forest → cleared brown patches  
> - **Flooding:** Normal terrain → water-like dark blue inundation
> - **Seasonal crop change:** Green crops → brown harvested / bare soil
> - **Fire / burn scar:** Vegetation → dark burnt patches
> - **No change (control):** Both images similar (natural variation only)
>
> This ensures the model learns to detect genuine visual differences. For production, replace with real Sentinel-2 multi-temporal data.

