### Section 2 — Bi-Temporal Dataset Collection

**~100 bi-temporal pairs** where each pair = ($T_1$ image, $T_2$ image) of the **same geographic area at different times**.

**$T_1$ (real):** Download EuroSAT images — serves as the "before" observation.

**$T_2$ (synthesised from $T_1$):** For each $T_1$, generate a realistic temporal change:

| Change Type | Source Classes | Transformation | Visual Effect |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Urbanisation** | Forest, Pasture, AnnualCrop | Add rectangular grey/white patches, edge structures | Green → built-up |
| **Deforestation** | Forest, HerbaceousVegetation | Replace green pixels with brown/tan soil | Dense green → bare earth |
| **Flooding** | River, Pasture, AnnualCrop | Expand dark blue regions, flatten texture | Normal → inundated |
| **Seasonal crop** | AnnualCrop, PermanentCrop | Shift green→brown, reduce NDVI proxy | Growing → harvested |
| **Fire / burn scar** | Forest, HerbaceousVegetation | Add dark charred patches, orange edges | Vegetation → burnt |
| **No change** | Any class | Minor brightness/contrast jitter only | Control pair |

~17 pairs per change type, total ~100 pairs.

